 # Diffuse Octree Rendering
 
-Also called: CPU Voxel Raycaster Octree Traversal
 
 ## Overview
-Diffuse Octree Rendering is an image-order raycasting technique that traverses an octree to locate the first leaf node containing data for each pixel, then computes surface lighting using a diffuse and Phong specular model with distance attenuation [S1, unofficial]. It differs from sibling methods by relying on a coarse-to-fine octree traversal to skip empty space entirely, rather than marching through a dense voxel grid or using ray-marching steps within occupied nodes [S1, unofficial].
